---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="DataTech Consulting and Contracting - AI Support Assistant for HVAC and Plumbing Companies"
  description="DataTech builds fixed-scope AI systems for local service businesses. Hero offer: an AI Support Assistant for HVAC and plumbing companies, $5,000 build plus $500/mo. Columbus, Ohio."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Your phones do not stop at 5 pm. Your intake should not either.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        DataTech builds a fixed-scope AI support assistant for HVAC and plumbing
        companies. It answers common questions, captures job details after hours
        and on busy days, and hands off to your team with a full summary.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Book a 20-minute fit call</a>
        <a class="btn secondary" href="/offers/ai-support-assistant/">See the offer</a>
      </p>
      <p>Fixed price: $5,000 build + $500/mo support. Stated up front, no discount programs.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The problem we fix first</h2>
      <p>
        For a local service business, the leak is usually not demand. It is calls
        missed after hours, calls missed while techs are on jobs, and enquiries
        that sit too long before anyone replies. Each one is a job someone else
        books.
      </p>
      <p>
        We start with that one workflow, build a system around it, and run it
        with your team. DataTech delivers fixed-scope builds, so you know what
        is included, what it costs, and when it launches before we start.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Five fixed-scope offers</h2>
      <p>Every offer has a set scope, a set price, and monthly support. Full detail is on the <a href="/offers/">offers page</a>.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="tag">Start here</span>
          <h3>AI Support Assistant</h3>
          <p class="price">$5,000 build + $500/mo</p>
          <p>Answers common questions and captures job details after hours and on busy days, with a full summary for your team.</p>
          <p><a href="/offers/ai-support-assistant/">Full offer</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Lead Intake</h3>
          <p class="price">$5,000 build + $500/mo</p>
          <p>Turns website, email, and message enquiries into structured leads with the details you need to quote and follow up.</p>
          <p><a href="/offers/#lead-intake">Details</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Call Intelligence</h3>
          <p class="price">$4,000 build + $400/mo</p>
          <p>Reviews your recorded calls and pulls out the jobs, complaints, and follow-ups that need a person.</p>
          <p><a href="/offers/#call-intelligence">Details</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Internal Knowledge Assistant</h3>
          <p class="price">$7,500 build + $750/mo</p>
          <p>Gives your team fast answers from your own manuals, policies, and job history, from sources you approve.</p>
          <p><a href="/offers/#internal-knowledge-assistant">Details</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Document Extraction</h3>
          <p class="price">$8,000 build + $750/mo</p>
          <p>Reads invoices, forms, and paperwork and puts the key fields into the system your team already uses.</p>
          <p><a href="/offers/#document-extraction">Details</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Something else?</h3>
          <p>Custom work is available when a fixed offer does not fit. We scope it the same way: in writing, with a price and a timeline before work starts.</p>
          <p><a href="/contact/">Talk it through</a></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Proof, from work we run ourselves</h2>
      <p>
        We do not publish client work without permission, so this site shows
        systems we own and operate. The same team runs automation for a
        Columbus rental portfolio and for a certified organic food business,
        and we built DataTech's own intake the same way we build for clients.
      </p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Rental portfolio, Columbus</h3>
          <p>Guest messaging, pricing support, and owner reporting across a rental portfolio we operate day to day.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Baked Well</h3>
          <p>Ordering, product, and operations systems for a certified organic food business we co-own and run.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>DataTech's own intake</h3>
          <p>Our enquiry path is a working lead intake system: structured questions, a clear summary, and a fast route to a person.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p><a href="/proof/">Read the proof pieces</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>About DataTech</h2>
      <p>
        DataTech is a founder-led technology delivery firm in Columbus, Ohio.
        We assess, we build, and we stay on for support after launch. Our
        founder sets the technical direction on every build. Delivery is
        managed day to day, and specialists are brought in by scope when a
        build needs them.
      </p>
      <p>
        We sell DataTech as the firm, not one person. If a system stops being
        true when one person is in a meeting, it was never a firm. We write
        scopes that hold up either way.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/about/">More about how we work</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Start with a fit call</h2>
      <p>
        The fit call is 20 minutes. We look at where calls and messages are
        missed, whether a fixed-scope build fixes it, and what it would take.
        If it is not a fit, we say so on the call.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Book a fit call</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
